__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Per-cycle snapshot-driven pipeline scratch files (bot/README.md "Snapshot-driven mode").
# Contain live account data (cash, positions, cost basis, tax lots) and/or an unapproved
# trade plan awaiting user confirmation — never committed; only the specific files listed
# in a plan/finalize result's `files_changed` are committed each cycle.
/snapshot.json
/plan_result*.json
/finalize_result.json
/price_fetch_plan.json
/fetched_bars.json
/price_cache_result.json

# Ad-hoc scratch files (report tables, PnL matching, email body assembly, etc.) built by
# the agent while composing the Step 9 email report each cycle — same rationale as above:
# live account data, never committed.
/scratch_*
/email_body.html
/email_body_plain.md

# Bucket-3 stateful data — formerly peak/prices.json, price_history/daily_bars.json,
# tax/realized_gains_by_year.json — is now dated snapshots/deltas on Google Drive, never
# git-tracked (CLAUDE.md Execution Mode Step 1 downloads the files a cycle needs, Step 8 uploads
# whatever new file(s) this cycle wrote). See bot/state_store.py (peak_prices,
# realized_gains_by_year — small, sharded/plain JSON, latest-snapshot-only) and
# bot/price_history_store.py (price history — gzip-compressed Parquet, windowed deltas). The
# local copies here are just this cycle's working copies. Note tax/paid_taxes_by_year.json
# (bucket 1, user-maintained, read-only) stays git-tracked — only the realized_gains_by_year/
# subdirectory under tax/ is ignored.
/peak/
/tax/realized_gains_by_year/
/price_history/

# Bucket-2 paper-trail rotation files: logs/trade_journal.md stays git-tracked (git already has
# its full history), but the rotated-out history_trade_journal-*.md files move to Google Drive
# only (CLAUDE.md Execution Mode Step 8) rather than git, since trade_journal.md's own git
# history already makes them redundant to keep in the repo.
/logs/history_trade_journal-*.md
